cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  The associated paper is under double-blind review, so authorship and venue
  metadata are intentionally withheld. Fill in the author, venue, year, DOI and
  license fields once the review process concludes, and delete this note.
title: >-
  MIRAGE: Privacy-Preserving Full-Body Identity Replacement with Consent-Based
  Restoration for Smart Glasses
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of MIRAGE, a three-tier split-execution system for
  full-body bystander privacy in smart-glasses video: fail-closed masking and
  encryption inside the wearable capture boundary, pose-conditioned synthetic
  human replacement driven only by identity-neutralised controls, and
  consent-scoped restoration of an individual track mediated by a trusted
  third party.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous (withheld for double-blind review)"
# repository-code is intentionally omitted while the paper is under double-blind review:
